    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for 2026-07-17 is anchored by the middle of the order, led by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.75). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** possesses the day's highest efficiency score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Anthony Kay (4.67 xERA) and an elevated role in the two-hole. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start, benefiting from a soft matchup against P. Lambert (4.28 xERA) and his consistent production at the top of the order. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Drake Baldwin** (71.33) round out our top-tier plays; **Jackson Merrill** is a high-upside asset given his balanced profile, while **Drake Baldwin** receives a massive 19% bump from the favorable skill profile of opposing starter Quantrill, though managers should monitor the 30% rain risk hovering over his contest.\n\nThe bench decision process was particularly rigorous today, with **Miguel Vargas** (43.50) narrowly missing the cut behind **Curtis Mead** (49.15). While **Miguel Vargas** boasts an elite xwOBA of 0.401, the optimizer favored **Curtis Mead** due to a +10% park factor advantage that outweighed the raw talent differential. **Heliot Ramos** fell below our 40.0 \"Below Floor\" threshold, largely due to a difficult matchup against B. Miller (2.85 xERA) and an unfavorable park projection, necessitating his exclusion to preserve our daily game caps. **Kyle Tucker** remains a steady start (65.24) against Gerrit Cole despite the high-caliber opponent, as his dynamic platoon splits and power ceiling are too valuable to sit in a 5x5 format where every home run counts toward our weekly totals.",
